<main id="main">
  <header class="page-hero" style="--page-hero-img:url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507838153414-b4b713384a76?w=1600&q=80');padding:80px 24px 50px">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right"></i><span>Class Policies</span></nav>
      <div class="page-hero-eyebrow"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-contract"></i>Crafting the Timeless in Time</div>
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Class <span class="highlight-gold">Policies</span></h1>
      <p class="page-hero-lede">The agreements that keep every MAM class focused, fair and rewarding. You also accept the relevant policy when you apply, and we email you a signed copy.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="legal">
    <p class="legal-intro">MAM Academy is committed to cultivating a structured, respectful and inspiring learning environment for every student. The policies below define the standards we uphold and the commitments we ask every student to honour. They are carefully designed to protect your learning experience, ensure fairness across all programmes, and give our instructors the conditions they need to teach at the highest level. Please read them carefully — you formally accept the applicable policy when you enrol, and we send you a confirmed copy by email.</p>

    <article class="policy-static" aria-label="Fees, registration and certification">
      <h2>Fees, Registration &amp; Certification</h2>
      <div class="sub">Applies to every student — online and onsite</div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">1</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Registration &amp; Onboarding</strong><span>A one-time, non-refundable registration fee of <span class="amt" data-amt-usd="5">$5</span> is required to open your student file and begin the onboarding process. This fee covers administrative processing, welcome materials and your initial placement into the Academy system. It is payable once and does not recur.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">2</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Mode of Learning</strong><span>Every student is classified at enrolment as either an <strong>Onsite</strong> or <strong>Online / Home</strong> learner. Your mode determines your programme structure, fee schedule and the policies applicable to your study. Your confirmed mode and fee are presented at checkout before payment is taken.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">3</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Certification Levels</strong><span>MAM Academy operates a four-tier progression framework: <strong>Level 1 — Pre-Certification</strong> (foundational skills), <strong>Level 2 — Certification I</strong> (intermediate competency), <strong>Level 3 — Pre-Diploma</strong> (advanced musicianship) and <strong>Level 4 — Diploma</strong> (professional mastery). All students progress sequentially through the tiers; your entry point is determined by the MAM Auditer placement assessment, conducted prior to or at the commencement of your programme.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">4</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Programme Options</strong><span>MAM Academy offers two principal programmes. The <strong>Certified Musician</strong> programme (from <span class="amt" data-amt-usd="240">$240</span>) provides intensive training in one chosen major specialisation — Contemporary, Classical or African Music — delivered at one hour per week over twelve weeks, available online or onsite. The <strong>Grand Musician</strong> programme (from <span class="amt" data-amt-usd="313">$313</span>) covers all three major specialisations concurrently, at one hour per specialisation weekly over twelve weeks, available online or onsite. Programme fees are confirmed at checkout.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">5</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Supporting Courses</strong><span>All students are required to undertake four supporting courses alongside their major programme: <em>Rhythm</em>, <em>APE (Art of Performance Excellence)</em>, <em>Meta Music</em> and <em>Theory of Music</em> (informed by the Trinity College London syllabus). Of these four, any two are fee-bearing and any two are complimentary. Specific course allocations are confirmed during enrolment.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">6</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Standard Programme Format</strong><span>The standard delivery format for the Certified Musician and Grand Musician programmes is twelve weeks at one hour per major course weekly, totalling twelve instructional hours per specialisation. Additional supporting courses are thirty minutes each in duration and are priced at fifty percent of the prevailing major-course fee.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">7</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Crash Programme</strong><span>The Crash Programme is a six-week accelerated format delivering the same core curriculum as the standard twelve-week programme within a condensed timeframe. It is available both online and onsite and is designed for students with scheduling constraints or prior foundational knowledge. All policies applicable to the standard programme apply equally to the Crash Programme.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">8</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Learning Resources</strong><span>Prescribed manuscripts are priced at <span class="amt" data-amt-usd="5">$5</span> each; handout materials carry a minimum production fee; and any required textbooks or supplementary materials are sold separately at the listed price. All learning resources are additional to programme fees and are not included in the cost of tuition unless explicitly stated otherwise.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">9</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>One-Time Events &amp; Special Sessions</strong><span>The Academy periodically offers stand-alone intensive events — including <a href="power-play">Power Play with Van. BOJA</a>, professional masterclasses, Cultural Architecture sessions and short-form music intensives — typically spanning one to two days. These are booked and invoiced separately from regular programme enrolments. Attendance at these events does not substitute for or count towards regular programme hours or assessments.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">10</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Payment Policy &amp; Non-Refundable Fees</strong><span>All payments to MAM Academy — including registration, programme tuition, supporting-course fees and resource charges — are final and non-refundable once your programme or onboarding process has commenced. This policy reflects the Academy's commitment of instructor time, studio resources and administrative capacity from the moment enrolment is confirmed. Exceptions apply only where applicable law expressly grants you a cancellation or refund right. Please refer to our <a href="terms">Terms of Service</a> for the complete refund position and a statement of your statutory rights.</span></div></div>
    </article>

    <div class="policy-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Policy type">
      <button class="policy-tab active" data-doc="online" role="tab" aria-selected="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-globe"></i> Online / Home</button>
      <button class="policy-tab" data-doc="onsite" role="tab" aria-selected="false"><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"></i> Onsite (Lagos)</button>
    </div>

    <div class="policy-currency" id="policyCurrency" role="region" aria-label="Display currency">
      <span class="pc-label">Show fines &amp; fees in</span>
      <div class="pc-switch" role="tablist" aria-label="Currency"><!-- built by JS --></div>
      <div class="pc-rate"><span class="pc-dot" id="pcDot"></span><span id="pcRateNote">Loading…</span></div>
    </div>

    <article class="policy-doc active" data-doc="online">
      <h2>Policy for Online / Home Classes</h2>
      <div class="sub">…crafting the Timeless into Time</div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">1</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Conducive Learning Environment</strong><span>Students are required to ensure that their learning environment is quiet, properly arranged and free from unnecessary interruptions for the full duration of every class. Adequate lighting, a stable internet connection and an accessible instrument or workstation must be in place before the class commences. A poor environment significantly diminishes the quality of instruction and may result in the class being paused or rescheduled at the student's expense.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">2</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>No Calls or Phone Use During Class</strong><span>Mobile phones must be set to silent or switched off before each session begins. Answering calls, engaging in messaging or using a phone for any unrelated purpose during class time is strictly prohibited. Compliance with this policy preserves the instructor's ability to deliver uninterrupted tuition and reflects the professional standards expected of every MAM student.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">3</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Class Readiness &amp; Punctuality</strong><span>Students must be fully prepared — instruments tuned, materials at hand and connection tested — at least fifteen minutes before the scheduled start time. Classes commence promptly; students who join late without prior notification will incur a late-arrival fine of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="500" data-fine-usd="0.50">₦500</span>. Where a delay is unavoidable, the instructor must be notified via WhatsApp or email at least two hours before the session. A maximum of two late arrivals is permitted per programme cycle before further disciplinary action is considered.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">4</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Assignment Compliance</strong><span>All assignments set by the instructor must be submitted by the agreed deadline. Assignments are a core component of the MAM learning framework and are designed to consolidate each week's lesson content. Late submissions — without a prior, approved extension — will attract a fine of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="1000" data-fine-usd="1">₦1,000</span> per occurrence. Habitual non-submission may be treated as a breach of the student's programme obligations.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">5</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Attendance &amp; Absence Notification</strong><span>Regular, consistent attendance is essential to your progress and to the integrity of your programme. If you are unable to attend a scheduled class, you must notify your instructor by phone or email at least twenty-four hours in advance. A maximum of two unplanned absences is permitted during a programme cycle. Any absence without adequate prior notice, or exceeding the permitted limit, will incur a fine of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="1000" data-fine-usd="1">₦1,000</span> per occurrence and may affect your eligibility for certification.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">6</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Class Rescheduling</strong><span>Requests to reschedule a session are considered only when submitted at least twenty-four hours before the class is due to begin. All approved reschedules are subject to an inconvenience fee of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="2000" data-fine-usd="2">₦2,000</span>, payable prior to the rescheduled session being confirmed. The Academy cannot guarantee the availability of the same instructor for a rescheduled session.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">7</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Weekly Progress Tracking &amp; Instructor Assignment</strong><span>MAM Academy maintains a progressive, written record of each student's development through weekly lesson remarks compiled by the instructor after every session. These remarks document technique, engagement, progress against the curriculum and any areas requiring focused attention. Based on this ongoing assessment, the Academy reserves the right to reassign a student to a different instructor at any time, without prior notice, where it is determined that such a change would better serve the student's learning outcomes, pace or programme requirements. Students are encouraged to focus on the curriculum and trust the Academy's professional judgement in instructor assignment.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">8</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Certification</strong><span>A certificate of completion is awarded to students who successfully pass the programme's revision exercises and final examination. The certificate is issued by MAM Academy upon confirmation of satisfactory performance across both assessments and will reflect the student's level, specialisation and the year of completion. Certificates are not issued where a student withdraws, fails to complete assessments or is found to have breached programme policies.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">9</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Daily Practice Assessment</strong><span>The Academy designates a daily practice window during which students may request a brief online review of their independent practice. These sessions are advisory, not instructional, and attendance is at the student's discretion. However, consistent engagement with daily practice is a strong predictor of progress and is actively encouraged as part of the MAM approach to development.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">10</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Device Requirements</strong><span>For online classes, students are required to have two internet-connected devices available during each session: one positioned to the left of the instrument, directed at the student's hands and instrument, and one directed at the student's face for clear visual communication. This dual-device configuration allows the instructor to observe both technique and engagement simultaneously, which is fundamental to the quality of online tuition at MAM Academy.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">11</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Payment Policy</strong><span>All fees paid to MAM Academy — including registration, tuition, supporting-course fees and resource charges — are non-refundable once your programme or onboarding has commenced. This reflects the Academy's commitment of instructor time and resources from the moment enrolment is confirmed. Exceptions apply solely where applicable law expressly confers a refund or cancellation right. Please see our <a href="terms">Terms of Service</a> for full details.</span></div></div>
    </article>

    <article class="policy-doc" data-doc="onsite">
      <h2>Policy for Onsite Classes</h2>
      <div class="sub">…crafting the Timeless into Time</div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">1</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Punctuality &amp; Arrival Protocol</strong><span>Students must arrive at the Academy premises at least thirty minutes before their scheduled class, in a calm and composed state of readiness. This allows time for instrument preparation, any necessary warm-up and the orderly transition between sessions. Arriving at or after the class start time without prior notification will incur a punctuality fine of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="1000" data-fine-usd="1">₦1,000</span>. Where late arrival is unavoidable, the student must notify the Academy by phone or message at least two hours before the class is due to begin.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">2</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Attendance &amp; Advance Notice</strong><span>Regular attendance is a core obligation of every enrolled student. If you are unable to attend a scheduled session for any reason, you must notify the Academy in writing — by email or WhatsApp — at least twenty-four hours in advance. Failure to provide timely notice will incur an absence fine of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="2000" data-fine-usd="2">₦2,000</span>. Repeated or unexplained absences will be reviewed by the Academic Director and may result in forfeiture of missed sessions without the right to make them up.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">3</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Assignment Compliance &amp; Daily Practice</strong><span>All assignments must be completed and submitted by the deadline communicated by the instructor. Late submission incurs a fine of <span class="fine" data-fine-ngn="1000" data-fine-usd="1">₦1,000</span> per occurrence. As part of the Academy's commitment to consistent progression, students are expected to document their daily practice and assignment progress through a brief one-minute video submission. These recordings support the instructor's weekly assessment and ensure that learning continues productively between sessions.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">4</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Mobile Phone Policy</strong><span>All mobile phones must be switched off or set to silent before entering the classroom or studio. The use of phones during instructional time — including messaging, social media, photography or calls — is strictly prohibited. The Academy's learning environment is designed to be distraction-free; breaches of this policy may result in removal from the session and a formal disciplinary note being placed on the student's record.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">5</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Decorum &amp; Participation</strong><span>Students are expected to conduct themselves with respect, professionalism and a genuine commitment to learning at all times whilst on Academy premises. Active, attentive participation in every class activity is required. Disruptive behaviour, disrespect towards instructors or fellow students, or consistent disengagement will be addressed by the Academy and may result in suspension from the programme without refund of fees.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">6</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Weekly Progress Tracking &amp; Instructor Assignment</strong><span>MAM Academy maintains a progressive, written record of each student's development through weekly lesson remarks compiled by the instructor following every session. These remarks form part of the student's official academic record and inform decisions about curriculum pacing, level progression and support requirements. Based on this ongoing assessment, the Academy reserves the right to reassign a student to a different instructor at any time, without prior notice, where such a change is judged to be in the student's best educational interest. Instructor assignment is an academic decision made solely by the Academy's management.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">7</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Certification</strong><span>A certificate of completion is awarded upon the successful completion of a thorough revision session followed by a formal examination. The certificate reflects the student's discipline, level of achievement and year of completion and is issued under the authority of MAM Academy. Students who fail to appear for assessments, withdraw from the programme or are found to have breached Academy policies during the programme cycle are not eligible for certification.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">8</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Daily Practice Commitment</strong><span>Structured, purposeful daily practice is the foundation of musical development and is an expectation of every student enrolled with MAM Academy. Students should set aside dedicated practice time each day to consolidate and internalise the concepts taught in class. The Academy's instructors monitor practice progress as part of the weekly lesson remark system, and consistent practice forms a component of the student's overall assessment.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><div class="rule-n">9</div><div class="rule-b"><strong>Payment Policy</strong><span>All fees paid to MAM Academy — including registration, tuition, supporting-course fees and resource charges — are non-refundable once your programme or onboarding has commenced, as the Academy commits instructor time, studio availability and administrative resources from the moment enrolment is confirmed. Exceptions apply only where applicable law expressly provides a refund or cancellation right. Please see our <a href="terms">Terms of Service</a> for the complete position and a statement of your statutory rights.</span></div></div>
    </article>

    <div class="policy-foot">
      By enrolling you join us in crafting a timeless legacy of growth, excellence and achievement.<br>
